  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">ACCP/Plan Sweden 2015 - 2018 Bridging - ACCP, African Children&apos;s Charter Project, New</narrative>
   <narrative xml:lang="SV">ACCP/Plan Sweden 2015 - 2018 Bridging</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="SV">Den afrikanska &quot;Children&apos;s Charter&quot; antogs 1999 av AU:s medlemsstater och har sedan dess ratificerats av 47 av AU:s 54 medlemsstater. 2001 etablerades en expertkommitte med uppgift att f&#xf6;lja upp medlemsstaternas &#xe5;tagande och granska rapportering. Expertkommitt&#xe9;n har dessv&#xe4;rre inte kunnat uppfylla sitt mandat p&#xe5; ett adekat s&#xe4;tt, framf&#xf6;r allt pga bristande resurser. 

Det h&#xe4;r projektet &#xe4;r en forts&#xe4;ttning p&#xe5; tidigare avtal. Det syftar till att ge teknisk assistans till expertkommitt&#xe9;n f&#xf6;r att p&#xe5; s&#xe5; s&#xe4;tt st&#xe4;rka upp uppf&#xf6;ljningen av Children&apos;s Charter. 

Erfarenheter fr&#xe5;n tidigare projektperiod &#xe4;r goda. Ambassadens avtalspart, Plan Sweden, har uppfyllt sina &#xe5;taganden och resultaten har varit i linje med plan.</narrative>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The African Children&apos;s Charter was adopted by the AU Member States in 1999 and has since been ratified by 47 of the AU 54 Member States. In 2001, an expert committee was set up to monitor the Member States&apos; commitment and review reports. Unfortunately, the Expert Committee has not been able to fulfill its mandate adequately, in particular due to lack of resources.

This project is a continuation of previous agreements. It aims to provide technical assistance to the Expert Committee in order to strengthen the follow-up of the Children&apos;s Charter.</narrative>
  </description>
  <description type="2">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">To facilitate the promotion and implementation of the ACRWC through a strengthened ACERWC; and increased engagement of African civil society organizations with the ACERWC.</narrative>
  </description>
